2026-10-05  Matevz Tadel  <matevz.tadel@ijs.si>

	configure now finds the libsets in the directories of the new option
	--libsetpath, default libsets, or takes a directory given as
	<LibSet>=<dir> in --libsets.  It records the directory of each libset,
	and the build reaches every libset through that directory.  The
	capitalised symlinks <LibSet> -> libsets/<LibSet> in the build directory
	are no longer read.

	* configure:
	* configure.rc:
	Added the option libsetpath, a ':' separated list of directories that
	hold libset directories.  A libset is looked up as <dir>/<LibSet>/Makefile
	in these directories in order.  The first one wins, and configure names
	the others.  An entry <LibSet>=<dir> in the libset list gives the
	directory of a libset explicitly.  The directory of a libset must be
	named after the libset.  <auto> takes all libsets in libsetpath.
	The directory of each libset, local or base, is recorded in
	LibName2LibSpecs as Dir.  The make runs in the libsets, the include
	flags, the reading of glass.list and FileStem use it.  The directory of
	a base libset comes from its manifest.  Makefile.config got LIBSET_DIRS,
	and its rules run make in the libset directories.
	make/make_config.inc is now written by both a full configure and
	--reconfigure.  It got a section with GLED_LIBSET_DIR_<LibSet> for each
	libset and GLED_LIBSET_INCL_<LibSet>, the include flags, for each local
	libset.  A full configure writes the file without that section first,
	because configure runs make in the libsets before resolving them.
	make/make_config.inc, make/make_rnr.inc and include/gled-config-build.h
	are written only when their content changes.  Before, every
	--reconfigure rewrote make_rnr.inc and gled-config-build.h, and the next
	make regenerated the glue, recompiled GledCore objects and relinked all
	libraries.
	build_config is written with sorted keys.
	The files that configure writes start with a line that names configure
	as their source.

	* make/make_base.inc:
	LIBSET_DIR is GLED_LIBSET_DIR_<LibSet> from make_config.inc, or the
	current directory for a libset that is not configured.

	* make/make_defs.inc:
	LOCALINCL takes GLED_LIBSET_INCL_<LibSet> from make_config.inc.
	Removed CPPFLAGSGEN, which ran gled_conf_dumper.pl on every make.

	* make/make_codegen.inc:
	* libexec/gled_manifest_writer.pl:
	The libset record of the manifest got the directory of the libset, from
	build_config.  The manifest is also remade when build_config or the
	writer changes.

	* Makefile:
	clean and distclean remove .depend_done in LIBSET_DIRS.

	* libexec/gled_config_writer.pl:
	bin/gled-config gets a line naming its generator after the '#!' line.

	* bin/gled-create:
	A new libset no longer gets a symlink in GLEDSYS.  The renderer header
	of a base glass is looked up in the libset directories recorded in
	build_config.

	* test/demos/run_demos.sh:
	* test/README.md:
	The demos are taken from $DEMOS_DIR, default $GLEDSYS/demos.  A macro
	that does not exist fails.  Before, it passed: gled printed a ROOT error
	for it and exited with 124, as a demo does after running.  An
	'Error in <' line in the output now fails a demo.

	* INSTALL:
	Described libsetpath and <LibSet>=<dir>.  After editing build_config,
	'./configure --reconfigure' writes make_config.inc from it.

2026-10-04  Matevz Tadel  <matevz.tadel@ijs.si>

	Added a manifest for each libset, lib/<LibSet>.manifest.  It holds the
	libset name, the libset ID, the required libsets and the glasses.
	configure now takes the libsets of the base builds given with --base
	from their manifests.  It no longer symlinks their directories into the
	build directory or runs their Makefiles.

	* libexec/gled_manifest_writer.pl:
	New script.  It writes the manifest of a libset to stdout from the
	REQUIRES_LIB_SETS of its Makefile, the libset ID in build_config and
	glass.list.  The manifest is a list of records such as
	'glass(ZImage, 1, Glasses/ZImage, rnr=ZImage)'.  'struct' lines at the
	top of the file name the fields of each record type once.

	* perllib/Gled_Records.pm:
	New module with the reader for such record files.  A value can be a
	word, a quoted string, a list, a hash or a nested record.  A trailing
	'@field' of a struct takes the remaining positional values, and a
	trailing '%field' takes the key=value pairs.  A wrong number of values,
	a duplicate key and a record without a struct are errors.

	* make/make_defs.inc:
	* make/make_codegen.inc:
	* make/make_targets.inc:
	Added the target manifest, which writes lib/<LibSet>.manifest from
	glass.list and the Makefile.  pre_depend and depend make it, and
	distclean removes it.

	* configure:
	A libset that is not in the build directory is looked up as
	<area>/lib/<LibSet>.manifest in the areas given with --base.  Its
	required libsets, its libset ID and its glasses for the resolver come
	from the manifest.  Its include path is <area>/<LibSet>.  Its bin, cfg,
	lib, libexec, macros and perllib files are linked into $GLEDSYS with
	gled_install_dirs.pl, the same directories as BUILD_INSTALL_DIRS in
	make/make_base.inc.  The resolver records the area of each such libset
	in BaseLibSetArea, and FileStem of its glasses points into that area.
	Removed the symlinking of base libset directories into the build
	directory.  The catalog of a base libset was read from the whole
	--base string joined with the libset name.  That path was wrong with
	more than one area, and for a base libset in the build directory
	itself.

	* configure.rc:
	* INSTALL:
	Described the lookup of base libsets by their manifests.

2026-10-03  Matevz Tadel  <matevz.tadel@ijs.si>

	Added test/ with the checks used to verify a built tree: dictionary
	selection and class checksums, demos, a multi-Saturn cluster and
	signal handling.  test/README.md describes the order in which to run
	them and what each one shows.

	* test/regress/dictsig.pl:
	* test/regress/dictsig.baseline:
	dictsig.pl prints what the rootcling dictionaries select: class infos,
	header names and class alternates, sorted.  The baseline covers the six
	base libsets at r3031.

	* test/regress/ckdump.C:
	* test/regress/cksum.baseline:
	ckdump.C writes the class version and checksum of the 148 glasses of
	the six base libsets.  The baseline was taken at r3006 and matches at
	r3031.

	* test/regress/deptest.C:
	Reports, for each libset that Var1 depends on, whether its base, View
	and Rnr_GL libraries are loaded.

	* test/demos/run_demos.sh:
	Runs demos for 22 s each.  A demo fails on an exit status other than
	124, on crash, heap-corruption or cling error lines in its output, or
	when the GUI message loop did not exit.  The exit status alone missed
	an abort in free() at shutdown and cling errors in nine macros.

	* test/cluster/run_cluster.py:
	* test/cluster/cluster_node.C:
	Start headless Saturns on localhost, or on several hosts with
	--hostpool, drive them through build, mirror, modify and dump phases,
	and compare what each Saturn holds.  Scenario basic has four Saturns;
	scenario scale has a sun with --fanout moons and a chain of --chain
	Saturns.  With --hostpool, the Saturns run through the site wrapper
	<remote-base>/run-in-container.sh, and --remote-base defaults to
	$GLED_T2_BASE.

	* test/signals/sigtest.sh:
	* test/signals/canv.C:
	* test/signals/late_loop.C:
	* test/signals/startup_loop.C:
	* test/signals/ctrlc_pty.py:
	sigtest.sh sends SIGTERM or SIGINT to gled when a macro has printed a
	given line and times the exit.  canv.C with --root-web server:<port>
	covers a signal during the start-up wait of a TWebCanvas, and
	late_loop.C a signal during a macro inside the event loop.
	ctrlc_pty.py types Ctrl-C on a pseudo-terminal while startup_loop.C
	runs under the ROOT prompt.

	* MANIFEST:
	Listed test/.

