2026-10-01  Matevz Tadel  <matevz.tadel@ijs.si>

	Replaced the per-class ROOT dictionaries with one dictionary per source
	directory of a libset, each generated by a single rootcling run.  A full
	build now runs rootcling 13 times instead of 191.

	* libexec/gled_mk_dict_gen.pl:
	Rewrote the script to generate the dictionary of one directory: it writes
	dict/<LibSet>_<Dir>_LinkDef.h and runs rootcling once over the dictionary
	headers of that directory.  The LinkDef holds the content of the
	hand-written <Dir>/LinkDef.h, followed by
	'class gled::ZLink<gled::<Glass>>' and 'class gled::<Glass>+' for every
	glass in glass.list that lives in the directory.  A rule in LinkDef.h that
	names a glass replaces the default '+' rule of that glass.  With
	'-t <tag>' the script builds an additional dictionary,
	dict/<LibSet>_<Dir>_<tag>_Dict.cc, from <Dir>/LinkDef_<tag>.h alone.  The
	catalog keys PragmaSuff, PrePragmas, Pragmas, PostPragmas, NoDefault and
	CINT_Opts are no longer read.  Removed the writing of an empty dictionary
	for headers without selection rules.

	* libexec/gled_mk_dict_dep.pl:
	Emit one dictionary rule and one dependency rule per dictionary instead of
	per class.  A directory with dictionary headers gets a dictionary when it
	holds glasses or a LinkDef.h, and one more for each LinkDef_<tag>.h.  A
	directory with dictionary headers and neither is an error.  The dictionary
	sources depend on the headers of their directory, on the LinkDef file,
	and for glass directories on glass.list.

	* make/make_base.inc:
	* make/make_targets.inc:
	Set DICT_AUTO_SRCS and DICT_AUTO_OBJS to the per-directory dictionaries,
	selected by the same rule as in gled_mk_dict_dep.pl.  Removed
	DICT_AUTO_HDRS, as rootcling writes no dictionary header.  Kept the
	LinkDef files out of BLESSED_HDRS and BASE_HDRS.  Pass the libset name to
	gled_mk_dict_dep.pl.

	* libexec/gled_cat_gen.pl:
	Stopped writing PragmaSuff into catalog.auto.

2026-09-07  Matevz Tadel  <matevz.tadel@ijs.si>

	Keep the build going with current ROOT (6.41) and C++20.

	* configure:
	Move generation of make/make_rnr.inc into write_make_rnr_inc() and call it
	for both a full configure and --reconfigure.  It used to be written only on
	a full configure, so --reconfigure silently kept stale renderer link lines.
	Link the GL renderer libraries against the new 'ftgl' external and hide its
	symbols with -Wl,--exclude-libs, so they cannot collide with the FTGL that
	ROOT re-exports from libRGL.so.  Escape ${LDFLAGS_LIBSETS} so it survives
	into the makefile instead of being eaten by perl interpolation -- as a
	result -Wl,--no-as-needed had never been applied to any *_Rnr_*.so.

	* libexec/gled_mk_dict_gen.pl:
	Write the empty translation unit ourselves when the generated LinkDef holds
	no selection rule at all (NoDefault with no Pragmas, e.g. GQueue).  Older
	rootcling accepted that and produced an empty dictionary; since 6.34 it is
	a hard error.  Also import Carp -- without it the croak on a failed
	rootcling died with a misleading "Can't call method croak without a
	package" instead of showing the real error.

	* make/make_base.inc:
	* make/make_targets.inc:
	Collect the *_rdict.pcm files rootcling drops next to the generated
	dictionary sources into lib/, where TCling looks for them, and remove them
	again on distclean.

	* perllib/Gled_Installer.pm:
	Reap stale symlinks on both install and uninstall.  'ln -sf' never cleans up
	after a file stops being produced, and the uninstall functions build their
	file list from the *source* directory, so neither could ever notice a
	leftover -- a symlink whose target had gone just sat there for good.
	reap_stale_symlinks() now drops dangling links from the destination, but only
	those pointing into the source directory being processed: ${GLEDSYS}/lib and
	friends are shared by every libset, and the other libsets' links must survive.
	Copies (rsync mode) carry no provenance and are left alone.

